@startuml
actor Developer
participant "Local shell\n(run-remote-benchmark.zsh)" as Script
participant "Git (lynx-journal)" as Git
participant "Maven" as Maven
participant "AWS S3\n(s3://{S3_BUCKET})" as S3
participant "GitHub\n(benchmark-as-a-service repo)\n(GitHub Actions)" as GH
participant "AWS Provisioner\n(in workflow)" as AWSProv
participant "Worker Instance\n(EC2/ECS/Fargate)" as Worker
participant "MongoDB\n(BaaS benchmark DB)" as MongoDB

Developer -> Script: run run-remote-benchmark.zsh [options]
Script -> Git: get_current_branch()
alt build not skipped
  Script -> Maven: mvn -f ../pom.xml clean package
  Maven --> Script: jmh-benchmarks.jar produced
  Script -> S3: upload jmh-benchmarks.jar -> s3://{bucket}/{branch}/jmh-benchmarks.jar
end
Script -> GH: gh workflow run benchmark-runner.yml --repo benchmark-as-a-service --ref {branch} \
  -f request_id=... -f results_path=... -f benchmark_path=s3://...
GH -> AWSProv: start/provision workers (using workflow steps)
AWSProv -> Worker: launch configured instance(s)
Worker -> S3: download jmh-benchmarks.jar
Worker -> Worker: run JMH benchmarks
Worker -> S3: upload outputs -> s3://{bucket}/{results_path}/
Worker -> MongoDB: insert benchmark metrics/docs
Worker -> GH: update job status (workflow logs & status)
GH -> Script: gh returns run id (Script polls with wait-for-gha-run.sh)
Script -> GH: gh run list / wait-for-gha-run.sh polls until run finishes
note right of Script: after completion:
Script -> MongoDB: mongosh "$BENCHMARK_DB_CONNECTION_STRING" --eval "$QUERY" (if defined)
MongoDB --> Script: query results
Script -> Developer: print results table and S3 console URL
@enduml